{"Cache key uses Python's built-in hash() of project IDs which is randomized per process, causing inconsistent cache hits/misses across workers and restarts - should use stable serialization instead": 0.9628981351852417, "_set_sample_rate_from_error_sampling accepts any truthy value and silently ignores conversion errors, which can set invalid sample rates (e.g., >1, negative, NaN) and produce incorrect/inconsistent weighting behavior": 0.8440821170806885, "upsampled_count is an internal aggregation but not marked private=True like other internal helpers (e.g. rounded_timestamp, column_hash), and the declared default_result_type should be 'integer' since the aggregation explicitly casts to Int64": 0.7635364532470703, "Line contains only indentation whitespace which triggers lint (e.g., W293) and creates noisy diffs - should be a truly blank line": 0.3339640200138092, "setUp overwrites self.user (which APITestCase uses as the logged-in user) after calling login_as, making the test harder to follow and potentially causing future helpers relying on self.user to behave unexpectedly - should use separate attributes for event tag users": 0.616701602935791, "Tag should use the dedicated event user created in setUp (e.g. self.event_user) instead of self.user to avoid confusion": 0.12412309646606445, "If self.user2 is renamed to a dedicated event user (e.g. self.event_user2), the tag reference should be updated to match the setUp attributes": 0.12837043404579163}